Let me include find_A plus maybe others with preconditions=[] too, but completion referencing objects is fine (objects as completion goal, not precondition). I'll keep minimal: one subgoal.\n\nPlan:\n{\"plan\":{\"subgoals\":[{\"subgoal_id\":\"find_A\",\"description\":\"scan conservatively to locate and confirm blue ball A\",\"preconditions\":[],\"completion\":[{\"object_id\":\"task:A\"}]}],\"branches\":[{\"on\":\"skill_stuck\",\"subgoal_id\":\"find_A\"}],\"recovery\":\"observe a fresh frame, then re-plan a safe scan direction or detour around cabinets\"},\"subgoal_id\":\"find_A\"}\n\nTool: turn(-0.5).\n\nWait, but is completion referencing task:A (an unconfirmed future object) acceptable? Completion is the goal to achieve; likely fine. The example uses point-001 which is a tracked point (confirmed-ish). Using task:A which is a task_target object_id — should be fine as a goal.\n\nLet me also reconsider: maybe I should do observe instead of turn to safely register plan, because if turn fails due to binding I lose. But I argued plan+turn is the flow. Let me commit to plan+turn but choose a small turn to be safe.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the possibility that the harness wants","role":"assistant"}}],"created":1794333008,"id":"chatcmpl-97551060-03b7-98e1-aba5-48907f590157","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":8192,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":8192,"text_tokens":0},"prompt_tokens":6308,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":6308},"total_tokens":14500}}